---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Vemor Consulting LLC"
  description="Privacy policy for Vemor Consulting LLC, covering how we handle data from our website, forms, and Vemor Comps reports."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="hero" style="min-height:0; padding-bottom:40px;">
    <span class="hero-tagline">Legal</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--text-muted);">Last updated: August 17, 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:800px;">
      <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
      <p>
        Vemor Consulting LLC ("Vemor," "we," "us") is a technology consulting
        company based in San Diego, California. This policy describes how we
        collect, use, and protect information through our website (vemor.ai) and
        services.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Form submissions:</strong> When you submit a form on our website
        (contact requests, Vemor Comps report requests, sample report requests),
        we collect the information you provide: your name, work email, law firm
        or organization, and the details of your request.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Analytics:</strong> We use Google Analytics 4 to collect
        anonymized usage data (pages visited, time on site, device type). This
        data is aggregated and does not personally identify you.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>No client confidential data via the site:</strong> Our website
        forms collect only the information necessary to fulfill your request. We
        do not collect confidential legal information, financial data, or
        sensitive personal information through this website.
      </p>

      <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p>
        We use the information you provide solely to respond to your inquiries,
        fulfill report requests, manage subscriptions, and improve our services.
        We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third
        parties for marketing purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Vemor Comps Data Sources</h2>
      <p>
        Vemor Comps reports are derived entirely from publicly filed documents on
        the California Department of Industrial Relations PAGA Case Search portal.
        No private, confidential, or non-public data is collected or used in the
        production of these reports.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Form submissions are retained for as long as necessary to fulfill your
        request and maintain the business relationship. You may request deletion
        of your personal information by contacting us at
        <a href="mailto:gio@vemor.ai" style="color:var(--gold);">gio@vemor.ai</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Cookies and Tracking</h2>
      <p>
        Our website uses cookies only for Google Analytics 4. We do not use
        advertising cookies, retargeting pixels, or third-party tracking beyond
        analytics. You can disable cookies in your browser settings at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take commercially reasonable steps to protect the information you
        provide, including encrypted transmission (HTTPS) and secure hosting
        through Netlify. However, no method of electronic transmission or
        storage is completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        Our website is hosted on Netlify. Form submissions are processed through
        Netlify Forms. Analytics are provided by Google Analytics 4. Each of
        these services has its own privacy policy governing their handling of
        data.
      </p>

      <h2>9. California Privacy Rights</h2>
      <p>
        California residents have the right to request disclosure of the
        categories and specific pieces of personal information we have collected,
        as well as the right to request deletion. Contact us at
        <a href="mailto:gio@vemor.ai" style="color:var(--gold);">gio@vemor.ai</a>
        to exercise these rights.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on
        this page with an updated date. Your continued use of our website after
        changes constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy may be directed to
        <a href="mailto:gio@vemor.ai" style="color:var(--gold);">gio@vemor.ai</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
